label sh_ch46:
    label .s1:

        $ set_window_tint(TINT_HISAO)

        call sisterhood_timeskip_broken

        scene bg satoujp_station
        show crowd
        show hanako emb_downtimid_cas_close at right

        play music music_dreamy fadein 4.0

        hi "I think that's Lilly and her father over there."
        "Hanako doesn't respond. It's really crowded at the train station right now, and she's trying to block out the rest of the world by hiding behind her long scarf and the collar of her thick coat."
        "Even though Christmas is not an official holiday here, there were still plenty of people who visited their family yesterday."
        hi "Lilly!"
        "I call out in the direction where I saw Lilly's distinct blonde hair."

        show hiroyuki bow at twoleft
        show lilly cane_cheerful_cas at left
        with charaenter

        "Moments later, I see someone wave at us. With Hanako clinging to my arm, I slowly make my way towards our friend."
        "As we reach Lilly and her father, they both greet us with a polite bow."

        show hanako emb_timid_cas_close
        show lilly cane_satisfied_cas
        show hiroyuki thinkinggesture
        with chchange

        hy "Miss Ikezawa. Mister Nakai. It is good to see you two again."
        hi "Merry Christmas Lilly. And you too, Mister Satou."
        ha "M-m-merry Christmas."
        li "Merry Christmas to the two of you as well. I'm really happy you're visiting today."

        show lilly cane_smileclosed_cas
        show hiroyuki serious
        with chchange

        hy "Let us not waste time standing around here. The car is parked not too far from here."
        hi "Great. It's kind of chilly today, so let's go."

        hide lilly
        hide hiroyuki
        hide hanako
        with charaexit

        "We follow Lilly and her father to the car, and a minute later, we're leaving the train station behind us."

        scene bg hiroyuki_car
        with locationskip

        hy "If the two of you desire to do some studying right now, I will not distract you with idle conversation."
        hi "How far is it from here?"
        hy "About 15 minutes."
        hi "Hmmm, might not be worth risking motion sickness over."
        hy "How about you, Miss Ikezawa?"
        ha "Umm...."
        "Hanako is a bit startled by Mister Satou suddenly addressing her, but then meekly shakes her head."
        hy "Just be sure to do your best to catch up when we get to the house."
        hi "Ah... Yes, sir."
        hy "If you wish as much peace and quiet as possible, you can use the guest rooms to study without anyone else around."
        hy "If you want to take the occasional break, my wife will be honored to bring you some tea and snacks once an hour or so. We will make sure not to disturb you until it is time for dinner."
        "I exchange a quick look with Hanako. My own parents were already pretty “encouraging” in getting us to devote as much time as possible on our studies, but Mister Satou seems even more driven."
        hi "We... ah... appreciate the effort, sir."
        "Lilly's father flashes us a wry smile."
        hy "I do feel a bit bad about having honored guests over and then pressuring them to spend about their entire stay engaged in an activity they are probably tired of by now."
        hy "But I speak from personal experience when I say that some of the most important days of your lives are less than four weeks away from you."
        hi "Personal experience?"
        "I guess so. Even though the company he worked at was a family company, it's doubtful he would have made it that far without having attended some prestigious university."
        hy "The days I spent studying for my own high school exams were some of the most stressful days of my life, and they were not very enjoyable, but the results were worth the stress and lack of sleep."
        hy "Sometimes you have to endure some short-term hardships in order to make a positive difference in the long run."
        hi "Enduring, huh?"
        hy "Yes. We Japanese have a proud tradition of being able to endure hardships with dignity and perseverance. It has made us some of the most resilient people in the world."
        hy "If you wonder whether all of the stress is worth it, think of the many people in this world who lack access to the educational opportunities you are being given. You will find that many hardships are relative."
        hi "That's a good point."
        hy "Also..."

        scene bg satoujp_guest
        with locationskip

        ka "Mister Nakai? I apologize for intruding, but I have brought you some herbal tea. Please enjoy."

        show karla basic_smileclosed_cas at center
        with charaenter

        "I turn around to look at the entrance of the guest room where I've been studying for the last two hours and look at the kimono-clad figure who just walked in carrying a tray."
        "I've seen Lilly's mother walking around in a business suit and in her sporty casual clothes, but seeing her in traditional Japanese clothes is another thing altogether."
        "Her sky-blue kimono constrasts very nicely with her blonde hair, and the way the fabric is flowing around her as she moves makes her appear very graceful. Her figure..."

        show karla basic_smug_cas
        with chchange

        ka "You know, if you keep staring like that I'll have no choice but to tell your girlfriend."

        play sound sfx_impact

        with vpunch

        "I instinctively flinch as I'm abruptly reminded that despite the change in clothes, the woman before me is still the same Karla Satou we met in that pub in Inverness."
        hi "I wasn't..."

        show karla basic_wink_cas
        with chchange

        ka "It's a joke, lad. I hope you're not angry."
        "I simply roll my eyes at that."
        "It wasn't so much Karla's remark that made me react, but simply the jarring effect of someone giving off such an elegant air at first before throwing out a blunt remark without warning."

        show karla basic_smile_cas
        with chchange

        hi "It's okay. I was wondering... Do you often wear traditional getups like these? And do you often greet your husband at the door the way you did when we arrived here? It kind of surprised me."

        show karla basic_sheepish_cas
        with chchange

        ka "Not really. They're beautiful and elegant, but not exactly practical. I also don't welcome my husband home every time he walks through the front door. These kinds of things are like one's favorite food. It only remains tasty if you don't eat it every day."

        show karla basic_sheepishclosed_cas
        with chchange

        "She hands me a bowl of very hot tea, which I put on the desk I'm seated at so it can cool down a bit. She then smiles sheepishly."
        ka "I suppose I'd better get going. I wouldn't want to distract you."
        hi "I'm actually thinking of taking a little break. You don't have to leave on my account."

        show karla basic_wink_cas
        with chchange

        ka "Well, if you don't mind a little company..."

        show karla basic_smile_cas at tworight
        with charamove

        play sound sfx_rustling
        with vpunch

        show karla basic_displeased_cas at right
        with charamove

        show karla basic_displeased_cas_close at right
        with chchange

        "She walks over to the bed, and I can't hold back a grin when I see her fumble with her kimono a bit before sitting down. She looks a bit annoyed at being caught out."

        show karla cross_wut_cas_close
        with chchange

        ka "Yeah, yeah, I guess I'm a little bit out of practice. It has been six years since I've worn one of these. My technique used to be much better."

        show karla cross_displeased_cas_close
        with chchange

        ka "But my husband hasn't complained, which is the important thing. And since settling here I've been focusing more on dusting off my Japanese than my kimono-wearing skills."
        "I can attest to that. When we first met her, Lilly's mother spoke with a pretty heavy accent. Her accent is still faintly noticable, but I could easily mistake it for some unfamiliar local accent if I didn't know her origins. I don't think my English will ever be that fluent."

        show karla basic_sheepish_cas_close
        with chchange

        hi "This is a gesture towards your husband then?"
        "She nods."

        show karla basic_confident_cas_close
        with chchange

        ka "My husband may have married a woman from Scotland, may have led a foreign branch of the company for years and may have even picked up a few western trains of thought here and there through his exposure to foreign cultures, but there's a part of him that will always remain traditionally Japanese, and he's always been very proud of his country and his culture."
        hi "That probably explained the speech we got on our way here about it being pretty much our civic duty to push ourselves as much as possible during these remaining four weeks in order to set the good example to the students and generations that come after us."

        show karla basic_laugh_cas_close
        with chchange

        "Karla lets out a bright laugh."
        ka "Sounds like you really got him going. He probably reminded you that he went through the same thing himself when he was younger, didn't he?"
        hi "Several times. What university did he attend? Did he make it in on his first try?"

        show karla basic_confident_cas_close
        with chchange

        "Karla smiles proudly."
        ka "The big T itself... Tokyo University—on his first try, too. Being at the top of his class throughout high school paid off."
        hi "Whoa! He didn't mention that."

        show karla basic_sheepish_cas_close
        with chchange

        ka "Can't say I'm surprised. He doesn't like boasting. He says it's un-Japanese."
        hi "I don't think we can compare to that. Man, that is impressive."

        show karla basic_ponder_cas_close
        with chchange

        ka "He always managed to push himself further than anyone else. That's why he succeeded. Anyway, try not to hold the tangent against him. He means well."

        show karla basic_pissed_cas_close
        with chchange

        ka "Although..."
        "Her face suddenly becomes frighteningly serious."
        ka "...it must be kind of ironic to be given a speech about enduring and pushing yourself by someone who endured and pushed himself all the way to Raigmore's Intensive Care ward."
        "I nearly choke on the sip of tea I just took. Karla didn't even try being subtle on that one."
        hi "You disagree with your husband's views?"

        show karla cross_ponder_cas_close
        with chchange

        "She slowly shakes her head."
        ka "I'm a little mixed on it. I agree with what he said in the car. The three of you really should give everything you've got to those upcoming exams, even if it's giving you a headache. The opportunity you're getting would indeed be a privilege in the eyes of many."

        show karla basic_ponder_cas_close
        with chchange

        ka "Anyway, there's a lot about the Japanese work ethic and perseverance that I admire. I respect how dedicated your people are to their jobs and how highly they regard their customers. I also admire the Japanese perseverance in the face of hardships."
        ka "If a neighborhood out here is ravaged by an earthquake, people simply keep going without complaining, or turning on each other, or looting other people's places. In a lot of other places in the world, chaos would probably erupt quickly."

        show karla basic_displeased_cas_close
        with chchange

        ka "But... Sometimes I feel those principles are taken too far."
        hi "Like when?"
        ka "Sometimes circumstances demand action rather than silent endurance."

        show karla basic_troubled_cas_close
        with chchange

        ka "Sometimes children being bullied by their peers, girls being bothered on crowded trains, or people in unhappy marriages endure their situation because they feel that that's what's being expected of them."
        ka "They believe that complaining or standing up for themselves would make people around them think less of them while I personally feel that those kinds of situations could be solved if the problems were highlighted instead of ignored."

        show karla basic_sad_cas_close
        with chchange

        ka "My husband's situation was a similar case. He felt the warning signs, but he just didn't speak up. Because he was taught from an early age that enduring without complaining was the proper thing to do, and he probably thought that there was no ‘honorable’ way out of his predicament."

        show karla basic_serious_cas_close
        with chchange

        "She looks straight at me like a police inspector interrogating a suspect."
        ka "What about you, Hisao?"
        "I'm not certain if I like the direction this discussion is headed in."
        hi "Me?"

        show karla basic_speak_cas_close
        with chchange

        ka "According to Lilly, you do little more than studying all day long these days. Are you still getting sufficient sleep each night? How about your daily exercise?"
        "I ditched my daily exercise weeks ago and I haven't had eight hours of sleep in days. But what choice do I have?"
        "It's easy for her to say I should take better care of myself, but I don't want to risk falling a few centimeters short of a passing grade over a few extra hours of sleep that I could have managed without."
        hi "I'm still doing okay so far. I realize that your husband also thought he could tough things out for a little longer too and endangered himself in the process, but I'm still making sure to take all my daily medication. I think they'll keep me going until things calm down a little bit."

        show karla cross_ponder_cas_close
        with chchange

        "She slowly nods her head."
        ka "Well, I hope you're right. Be sure to see a nurse if something feels off."
        hi "I will."

        show karla basic_wink_cas_close
        with chchange

        "She grins."
        ka "Attaboy."
        hi "By the way, how has your husband been doing? Has he had any more trouble?"

        show karla basic_smile_cas_close
        with chchange

        "She brightens up a little bit."
        ka "He's doing much better right now, though I'm sure he'll be happy to tell you the details himself."
        ka "At the beginning, it was really tough for him though. At first, every single tingle in his stomach or chest made him wonder if another attack was coming up. Makes you really paranoid."
        ka "Lilly said that it was not uncommon for people recovering from a heart attack to feel that way."
        "I smirk a bit at that. Karla notices my expression and chuckles."

        show karla basic_smug_cas_close
        with chchange

        ka "Makes me wonder about her sources."

        show karla basic_sheepish_cas_close
        with chchange

        "I shrug my shoulders."
        hi "After we got back from Scotland, Hanako suddenly started getting unusually curious about... things. Or maybe she was always curious, but until then she was simply too shy to ask. Sometimes she'd even ask me a question out of the blue."

        show karla basic_cheerful_cas_close
        with chchange

        ka "And you decided to play along with the game that Lilly and Hanako were playing there?"

        show karla basic_smileclosed_cas_close
        with chchange

        hi "Well, it seemed to make Hanako happy. Besides, I never got the impression that she was doing it purely for the sake of passing it on to Lilly during their daily phone calls."
        hi "She always looked extremely sincere while listening to whatever I had to say about... the subject. I think she genuinely wanted to know how I felt about things. And she's always been a very good listener."

        nvl clear
        nvl show dissolve

        n "It probably helped me too. I've always been very reluctant to talk about my condition. And more than a little uncomfortable too."
        n "{vspace=30}But the knowledge that there was someone out there, someone related to one of my best friends no less, who might be drawing strength from my thoughts and impressions was a very effective push."
        n "And it also helped that Hanako never tried to force things. Whenever I started feeling uncomfortable, she'd never fail to soothe my nerves. She'd take my hand in hers, or snuggle up to me, or give me a soft kiss accompanied by that warm smile of hers, or let me rest my head in her lap while she ran her fingers through my hair."
        n "{vspace=30}True to her usual ways, she'd hardly ever speak while doing all of that, but I always felt stronger and more at ease afterwards. She was such a sweetheart during those moments. The two of us probably got a lot closer during that time."

        nvl hide dissolve

        show karla basic_smile_cas_close
        with chchange

        ka "I think it helped a lot. Lilly often used your example to remind my husband that it was possible to go through something like that and pick yourself up afterwards."
        ka "So... thanks for that. I think we as a family owe you one."
        "It feels kind of weird to hear that my life has been used to offer comfort to a recovering heart patient. They should have seen me the way I was before Hanako and Lilly entered my life."
        hi "I mostly bounced back thanks to Hanako and your daughter. I'm happy I could do something back for Lilly."
        "I sigh."
        hi "If only it was that easy to help Hanako get back on her feet."

        show karla basic_speak_cas_close
        with chchange

        show karla basic_distant_cas_close
        with charachangealways

        "Karla opens her mouth to say something, but then seems to think the better of it."

        show karla basic_distant_cas
        with charamove

        "After a few quiet seconds, she gets up."
        ka "I'm sure she'll be fine in the end."
        hi "Well..."

        show karla basic_confident_cas
        with chchange

        ka "I'd better get going now. Gotta start preparing dinner. You try to do a bit more studying, okay?"
        hi "Yes, ma'am."

        stop music fadeout 2.0

        if _in_replay:
            return

    label .s2:

        $ set_window_tint(TINT_HISAO)

        scene bg satoujp_guest_ni
        with locationskip

        play music music_happiness fadein 4.0

        hi "Come in."

        show lilly cane_smileclosed_cas
        with charaenter

        "I turn around as I answer the knock on the door and it slowly opens, revealing Lilly standing in the doorway."
        li "Hisao, have you been able to get a lot of studying done?"
        hi "I think so. I'm about ready for a break."

        show lilly cane_smile_cas
        with chchange

        li "Mother has just informed us that dinner is ready. We were hoping you could join us downstairs."
        hi "I'd love to. I think I've managed to work up quite the appetite over the last few hours."

        show lilly cane_smileclosed_cas at offscreenright
        with charamove

        hide lilly
        with None

        "I put a bookmark in my science book to mark the spot where I'll be picking things up after dinner and leave the guest room."

        scene bg satoujp_stairs
        show lilly cane_smileclosed_cas_close at left
        show hanako emb_downtimid_cas_nohat_close at right
        with charaenter

        "Beyond the doorway, Lilly and Hanako are waiting for me. I look at Hanako, who's fidgeting with one of the sleeves of the thick (and slightly too large) sweater she's wearing."
        hi "Hey, Hanako. How's your studying coming along?"

        show hanako emb_timid_cas_nohat_close
        with chchange

        ha "N-not t-too bad."

        show lilly cane_smile_cas_close
        with chchange

        li "It's good to hear that we've all done a good amount of studying."

        show lilly basic_satisfied_cas_close
        with chchange

        li "Come, let's not keep Father and Mother waiting for too long."

        scene bg satoujp_diningroom_ni
        show hiroyuki smileclosed at center
        show karla basic_sheepish_cas at tworight
        with locationchange

        "We follow Lilly down the stairs and into the dining area where her parents are waiting for us at a carefully laid table."

        show hiroyuki thinkinggesture
        with chchange

        show hiroyuki thinking
        with charachangealways

        show hanako emb_timid_cas_nohat_close at left
        with charaenter

        show lilly basic_smile_cas at right:
            xzoom -1.0
        with charaenter

        "Mister Satou, who's sitting at the head of the table, gives us a friendly nod and motions Hanako and me to sit down on his left. Lilly is delegated to the seat next to her mother on his right."
        "I wonder if they picked this arrangement because it makes certain that everyone at the table is facing Hanako's left side, hopefully putting her at ease a little bit."

        show karla cross_ponder_cas
        with chchange

        show karla basic_ponder_cas
        with charachangealways

        "After we sit down, Karla takes two bowls, fills each with hot miso soup, and puts them in front of us before serving her husband and her daughter."

        show hiroyuki smileclosed
        show karla basic_smileclosed_cas
        show lilly basic_cheerful_cas
        show hanako emb_downmeek_cas_nohat_close
        with chchange

        hi "The soup smells delicious, Mrs. Satou."

        show hiroyuki thinking
        show lilly basic_smileclosed_cas
        show karla basic_confident_cas
        with chchange

        ka "Thanks Hisao. This meal is probably one of the more unorthodox ones I've made in recent memory, so I'm keeping my fingers crossed that you'll find it tasty."
        hi "Unorthodox? The soup smells good, but I don't smell anything unorthodox about it."

        show karla basic_cheerful_cas
        with chchange

        "Karla grins."
        ka "The're nothing unusual about a meal with miso soup, noodles and cooked rice, but I've also prepared a western-style turkey for the main course and a Scottish dundee cake for dessert."
        hi "That's a... pretty unusual combination."

        show karla basic_sheepish_cas
        with chchange

        ka "Think of it as a multi-cultural meal. I came up with the idea while I was visiting a few of my friends in Inverness, and we talked about what each of us was planning for Christmas."
        hi "Do you often visit your country of birth these days?"

        show lilly basic_weaksmile_cas
        show karla basic_confident_cas
        with chchange

        ka "About every 5 to 6 weeks or so. Though I usually don't stay longer than a couple of days. Just long enough to drop by the head office for a few days and hang out with my Scottish friends."

        show hanako emb_timid_cas_nohat_close
        with chchange

        hi "Are you still employed at the company?"

        show hiroyuki serious
        show karla cross_ponder_cas
        with chchange

        ka "Not officially. But I drop by there whenever I'm in the area so I can keep an eye on how things are going, remain informed about the going-ons there, keep my ear close to the grapevine, and see if there are any conflicts or misunderstandings between the staff and the new management that I can help smooth over."

        show hiroyuki speak
        with chchange

        hy "There is also value in getting updates on the company's condition from sources other than the official channels, especially since the board of directors is so far removed from head office's geographical location."
        hi "How are you finding your new position on the board, sir?"

        show hiroyuki smileclosed
        show karla basic_sheepish_cas
        show lilly basic_smileclosed_cas
        with chchange

        "Lilly's father lets out a soft “hmmm”."

        show hiroyuki serious
        show karla basic_smile_cas
        with chchange

        hy "I am honored to be a member there, but to be honest, meetings are so infrequent that I would end up with a lot of spare time if that were to be the only job I got involved in."
        hy "Fortunately, that will not remain the case for much longer."
        hi "Have you found a new job, then?"

        show hiroyuki smileclosed
        with chchange

        "A subtle smile appears on Mister Satou's face for a moment."

        show karla basic_cheerful_cas
        show lilly basic_cheerful_cas
        with chchange

        hy "I will remain a member of the Satou board of directors, but early next year, I will also join the ranks of another company."
        "Karla grins."

        show hiroyuki awkward
        show karla basic_smug_cas
        show lilly basic_surprised_cas
        with chchange

        ka "The old boy network came to the rescue."

        show hiroyuki stern
        show karla basic_sheepishclosed_cas
        show lilly basic_weaksmile_cas
        with chchange

        "Lilly's father gives his wife a short admonishing stare, but then continues."

        show hiroyuki thinking
        show lilly basic_smileclosed_cas
        with chchange

        hy "My successor at head office knew someone from his university days who works at the upper management of another company and he was willing to put in a good word for me."
        hi "What kind of company?"

        show hiroyuki speak
        show karla basic_smile_cas
        show lilly basic_smile_cas
        show hanako emb_downmeek_cas_nohat_close
        with chchange

        hy "They are a major book publisher in Japan."
        hy "The department I will be given a managing role in is responsible for analyzing the foreign market, determining which books would be viable to localize in other languages, coordinating the translators doing the localizations, and then helping out with the marketing abroad."

        show karla basic_wink_cas
        show lilly basic_cheerful_cas
        with chchange

        ka "In other words: the ideal place for an avid reader who is well-traveled. I'm sure he'll do very well."

        show hanako emb_meek_cas_nohat_close
        show karla basic_smileclosed_cas
        with chchange

        hi "That sounds like a very enjoyable job."
        ha "Yes. C-congratulations."

        show hiroyuki thinkinggesture
        show hanako emb_downmeek_cas_nohat_close
        show lilly basic_smileclosed_cas
        with chchange

        hy "Thank you. I have always been more interested in books than in medical equipment, so it sounds like an enjoyable occupation although it is, of course, a bit of a demotion when you consider my previous position."

        show hiroyuki thinking
        show hanako emb_timid_cas_nohat_close
        show karla basic_confused_cas
        with chchange

        ka "Dear, your current position is member..."

        show hiroyuki speak
        with chchange

        hy "Ahem...junior member..."

        show hiroyuki serious
        show karla basic_speak_cas
        with chchange

        ka "...junior member of the board of directors of an international corporation, which is a step up from CEO who got appointed by that board to manage things at head office. This new job is simply something you're doing on the side."

        show karla basic_sheepish_cas
        with chchange

        hy "That is not a bad way of looking at it, although I will not be able to afford allowing my future colleagues to see me like that."
        hy "If they feel I am merely doing my job ‘on the side’, as you phrased it, they will not respect my input. I will have to pull my weight."

        show lilly basic_oops_cas
        show karla cross_ponder_cas
        with chchange

        "Lilly looks a little uneasy at her father's words."

        show lilly basic_listen_cas
        show hanako emb_downtimid_cas_nohat_close
        show karla basic_distant_cas
        with chchange

        li "I just hope you'll remain mindful of your health, Father."

        show hiroyuki thinking
        with chchange

        hy "I have no intention of getting hospitalized again, Lilly. I will make certain to remain under the watch of a physician who will be given permission to share his findings with your mother if he feels it necessary."
        hy "I will also not be working full-time—yet—though the fact that I still have to be available for meetings of our company's board of directors every now and then is the officially stated reason for that."

        show lilly basic_weaksmile_cas
        show hanako emb_downmeek_cas_nohat_close
        show karla basic_sheepish_cas
        with chchange

        "Karla gives a satisfied nod."
        ka "That does put my mind at ease."

        show hiroyuki smile
        show lilly basic_smile_cas
        show karla basic_smile_cas
        with chchange

        hy "Good. Then let us continue with this exquisite meal."

        scene bg satoujp_diningroom_ni
        show hiroyuki thinking at center
        show karla basic_cheerful_cas at tworight
        show lilly basic_smile_cas at right:
            xzoom -1.0
        show hanako emb_downmeek_cas_nohat_close at left
        with shorttimeskip

        ka "Anybody up for another slice of dundee cake?"
        "No response. I was already pretty full before we got to dessert, and if I eat any more, I'll be guaranteed to contract a stomach ache. I might not be the only one feeling that way."

        show hiroyuki smileclosed
        show karla basic_sheepish_cas
        with chchange

        hy "I have the impression that our upcoming graduates are about ready to get back to their books."
        "I suppose that's our cue."

        show lilly basic_smileclosed_cas
        show hanako emb_meek_cas_nohat_close
        with chchange

        li "Thank you for the meal."
        ha "Yes. T-thanks."
        hi "We will be sure to study as hard as we can until it's time to leave."

        show hiroyuki thinking
        show karla basic_smile_cas
        with chchange

        hy "That is good to hear. Perhaps, Lilly, I can supply you with some additional motivation."

        show lilly basic_surprised_cas
        show hanako emb_timid_cas_nohat_close
        with chchange

        li "Hmmm?"

        show hiroyuki serious
        with chchange

        "Mister Satou straightens himself out and pauses for a moment for dramatic effect."
        hy "I have been thinking about the request you made some time ago. About... living accommodations."

        show lilly basic_emb_cas
        with chchange

        li "Oh..."
        "Lilly lets out a small gasp. It's obvious that she didn't expect this subject to suddenly pop up."

        show hiroyuki thinking
        show karla basic_sheepish_cas
        with chchange

        hy "While a part of me is still skeptical, I have to decided to procur an apartment for you to use and give you the opportunity to live on your own, provided that you pass your exams."
